    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/director-business-partnering-in-richmond-au-jid-573": {
      "title": "Director, Business Partnering",
      "description": "Director, Business Partnering Division Operations __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Richmond, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1910P Apply Shortlist Full-time, 5 year fixed term contract senior position Hawkesbury and Parramatta South campuses with flexible working arrangements Competitive senior-level remuneration, commensurate with experience. Lead strategic people partnering for University leaders, translating priorities into workforce plans, capability and performance outcomes. The Opportunity You will lead a contemporary, people-focused business partnering model that connects University priorities with practical workforce strategies. Working closely with executive and senior leaders, you will anticipate complex workforce challenges and strengthen organisational performance, leadership capability and employee experience. You will guide strategic workforce planning across workforce shape, critical capabilities, succession, performance, engagement and change. By combining portfolio intelligence, workforce data, scenario analysis and external insights, you will identify emerging risks and provide clear recommendations that support executive decision-making. As a member of the People and Culture Leadership Team, you will coordinate integrated solutions across specialist People and Culture functions. You will also provide strategic oversight of employment and industrial relations, lead remuneration and benefits, and ensure reward, job architecture and classification frameworks support workforce strategy, equity, governance and financial sustainability. What Success Looks Like: Establish a consistent business partnering model with clear service standards, portfolio alignment, escalation pathways and measures of impact. Translate University and divisional priorities into integrated workforce plans that address capability, succession, performance and change. Strengthen leadership accountability, decision-making and people management practices across the University. Provide strategic oversight of complex employment and industrial relations matters, supporting sound governance and risk management. Align remuneration, reward, benefits and workforce architecture with organisational strategy, equity and sustainability. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You A relevant tertiary qualification in Business, Commerce, Human Resources Management, Industrial Relations, Law, Psychology or a related discipline, supported by extensive experience in a large and complex organisation. Demonstrated expertise in employment, industrial and workplace relations, including complex matters, negotiations, organisational risk and employer representation. Demonstrated experience leading and developing People and Culture Business Partnering teams to provide strategic, pragmatic and consistent advice. Strong analytical, critical-thinking and problem-solving skills, with the ability to translate complex information into practical and sustainable solutions. High-level leadership and negotiation capability, together with expertise in remuneration, reward, benefits, job evaluation and classification frameworks. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Angy Dinevska, Chief People Officer via A.Dinevska@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1910P Closing Date: 11:59pm, Wednesday 21st October 2026 Working Rights: You must provide evidence of full-time working rights in Australia at application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Lecturer (Chemistry) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Engineering, Computing & Science (U73K) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Ongoing position at Academic Level B.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Teach chemistry, d Reference 4ee3304b-a192-44f8-be8d-507908406a1f Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Lecturer in Finance Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Soc.Sciences,Art,Business,Education&Law (U73L) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Fixed-Term position to 30 November 2027 at Academic Level B.Parramatta City Campus.Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape future finance graduates thr Reference 11605e60-54ae-40be-a995-73258a97790b Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Manager, IT Service Management - Digital Services Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead enterprise IT servi Reference 77653bd1-243b-49da-bb96-0a480288384a Exp