    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/mobile-systems-engineer-in-penrith-au-jid-574": {
      "title": "Mobile Systems Engineer",
      "description": "Mobile Systems Engineer Division Provost __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Penrith, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1897Z Apply Shortlist Full-time, 12 Month Fixed-Term position at HEW Level 7. Penrith Campus with Flexible working arrangements. Salary: $108,659 – $117,202 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Design, integrate and operate fixed-wing aircraft and drone platforms that support advanced research, testing and data collection. The Opportunity You will provide specialist engineering expertise to support the design, fabrication, integration, testing and operation of fixed-wing aircraft and drone platforms used in ICNS research. You will develop and deploy custom airborne platforms, integrating sensors, research equipment, payloads, flight controllers, communication systems and processing interfaces. Your work will support autonomous aircraft, neuromorphic sensing technologies, drone-detection systems and agricultural drone applications. You will translate research and project requirements into practical engineering solutions, conduct ground and flight testing, and maintain the documentation and procedures needed for safe, compliant operations. You will also provide technical guidance to staff using specialised manufacturing equipment and processes. What Success Looks Like: Design and develop reliable fixed-wing aircraft and drone platforms for research, testing and data collection. Integrate sensors, payloads, flight controllers and processing systems into safe, functional airborne platforms. Deliver flight-control, communication and processing interfaces that support autonomous and coordinated operations. Plan and conduct ground and flight testing to verify performance, reliability and project outcomes. Maintain safe, compliant aircraft operations and complete technical and engineering records. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You A degree in Mechanical, Aeronautical or Aerospace Engineering, or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience, education and training. Demonstrated experience designing, fabricating, assembling and operating fixed-wing aircraft and drone platforms. Experience using computer-aided design and manufacturing technologies to produce aircraft components and systems. Demonstrated capability integrating sensors, payloads, flight controllers and associated systems into airborne platforms. Strong analytical, problem-solving, project management and communication skills, with experience delivering technical projects within agreed timeframes. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Gregory Cohen, Director, International Centre for Neuromorphic Systems via G.Cohen@westernsydney.edu.au or Ashay Dhamdhere, Engineering Projects Team Leader, ICNS via A.Dhamdhere@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1897Z. Closing Date: 11:59pm, Tuesday 20 October 2026. Working Rights: You must provide evidence of full-time working rights in Australia at application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About ICNS The International Centre for Neuromorphic Systems (ICNS) is a Centre within the MARCS Institute for Brain, Behaviour and Development at Western Sydney University. ICNS is explicitly interdisciplinary, bringing together expertise in electrical engineering, computer science, signal processing and neuroscience. The Centre focuses on developing neuromorphic engineering solutions to address real-world challenges and existing problems. ICNS has strong international partnerships and collaborations across the global neuromorphic engineering community. Further information is available on the ICNS website: http://westernsydney.edu.au/icns About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Lecturer (Chemistry) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Engineering, Computing & Science (U73K) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Ongoing position at Academic Level B.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Teach chemistry, d Reference 4ee3304b-a192-44f8-be8d-507908406a1f Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Lecturer in Finance Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Soc.Sciences,Art,Business,Education&Law (U73L) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Fixed-Term position to 30 November 2027 at Academic Level B.Parramatta City Campus.Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape future finance graduates thr Reference 11605e60-54ae-40be-a995-73258a97790b Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Manager, IT Service Management - Digital Services Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead enterprise IT servi Reference 77653bd1-243b-49da-bb96-0a480288384a Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Remuneration & Benefits Specialist Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury and Parramatta South campuses with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead remuner Reference 0ac8e10e-d401-4a3e-9b53-fc5fc92fbefe Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Placement Officer Salary Location Goulburn, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Goulburn Business Unit Faculty of Soc.Sciences,Art,Business,Education&Law (U73L) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 6.Goulburn campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $99,159 – $106,284 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Coordinate student placements with Reference 310234af-aaad-4187-a68b-a86fa24531ef Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Director, Global Program Liaison Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Global Partnerships & Transnational Education (U73N) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Senior Description Full-time, Senior Position on a 5-Year Fixed-Term Contract.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements.Competitive senior-level remuneration, commensurate with experience.Lead the gove Reference 6a621932-48ef-4fb5-b7ef-67af0297c0eb Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Manager, Industry Innovation Salary Location Bankstown, AU Di