    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/associate-professor-of-nursing-evidence-and-implementation-science-in-campbelltown-au-jid-376": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Nursing (Evidence and Implementation Science)",
      "description": "Associate Professor of Nursing (Evidence and Implementation Science) Division Provost __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Campbelltown, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1290M Apply Shortlist Full-time, Ongoing position at Academic Level D. Campbelltown Campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $182,520 – $200,625 plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead implementation science that translates nursing evidence into sustained improvements in care, education and community health . The Opportunity You will provide leadership in education, research and capacity development in implementation science and evidence-based practice within the School of Nursing and Midwifery. You will strengthen the School’s ability to translate evidence into frontline nursing and midwifery practice, with a clear focus on the communities of Greater Western Sydney. You will teach evidence-based practice and implementation science methods across undergraduate and postgraduate programs, develop new course offerings in this specialisation, and build capability in translation, de-implementation, scale-up and sustainment of nurse-led interventions. You will also supervise higher degree research candidates and mentor clinician-researchers developing combined clinical and research careers. You will connect digital health and AI-enabled care models with practical implementation in resource-constrained settings. Working across Campbelltown Campus and the Lang Walker AO Medical Research Building, you will collaborate with the Translational Health Research Institute, the local health district and industry partners to strengthen research translation, clinical partnerships and measurable impact. What Success Looks Like: A stronger School-wide capability in implementation science and evidence-based practice. High-quality teaching and new course offerings across undergraduate and postgraduate programs. Research that advances translation, de-implementation, scale-up and sustainment of nurse-led interventions. Effective evaluation of how digital health and AI-enabled care models are adopted in frontline practice. A strong pipeline of HDR supervision, clinician-researcher mentorship and partner-engaged research. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You A PhD in a related discipline and demonstrated expertise within the nursing profession and specifically in implementation science and evidence-based practice. Proven success in designing and delivering undergraduate and postgraduate learning experiences using contemporary pedagogical approaches and educational technologies. A strong track record of research leadership, including leading projects, supervising postgraduate researchers and contributing to the advancement of nursing knowledge and implementation science and evidence-based practice. Highly developed interpersonal and collaboration skills with the ability to build productive relationships across academia, industry and professional networks. A passion for mentoring others and fostering a culture of excellence in teaching, research and engagement. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. ​​​ Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Professor Caleb Ferguson, Dean, School of Nursing and Midwifery via C.Ferguson@westernsydney.edu.au Please include the job reference code REF1290M. Closing Date: 11:59pm, 20th October 2026. Working Rights: You must provide evidence of full-time working rights in Australia at application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Lecturer (Chemistry) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Engineering, Computing & Science (U73K) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Ongoing position at Academic Level B.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Teach chemistry, d Reference 4ee3304b-a192-44f8-be8d-507908406a1f Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Lecturer in Finance Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Soc.Sciences,Art,Business,Education&Law (U73L) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Fixed-Term position to 30 November 2027 at Academic Level B.Parramatta City Campus.Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape future finance graduates thr Reference 11605e60-54ae-40be-a995-73258a97790b Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Manager, IT Service Management - Digital Services Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead enterprise IT servi Reference 77653bd1-243b-49da-bb96-0a480288384a Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read 