 of research, engagement, and innovation initiatives. Responsibilities include providing administrative and project support, maintaining records, spreadsheets and databases, coordinating calendars and meetings, preparing presentations, reports and correspondence, and assisting with the planning and delivery of events, workshops, and activities that support Indigenous research and other divisional priorities. Parramatta City The College: Based at our Parramatta City campus, you'll support students on their journey at Western. Gain practical experience managing records, coordinating meetings and events, preparing documents and correspondence, and providing administrative support to a busy team. Parramatta South: Faculty of Social Sciences, Arts, Business, Education and Law (SABEL): Located at our Parramatta South campus, you'll gain hands-on experience supporting the daily operations of one of the University's largest faculties. Duties include administration, event coordination, record management, preparing documentation, and assisting staff, students, and visitors. Division of the Provost: Based at our Parramatta South campus, you'll work within a central division that supports the University's academic faculties and schools. Gain exposure to university-wide operations in a senior executive office while developing practical skills in administration, calendar management, event coordination, communication and stakeholder support. Applicants will be asked to rank the above opportunities across the Western Sydney University campuses in order of preference as part of the application process. For further information, please refer to the Position Description. About You To be considered for this opportunity, you must: Identify as Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander Person. Have completed a year 9 level of schooling or equivalent. Have an interest in general business administration duties. Display a commitment to enrol and complete a Certificate III in Business (Administration) traineeship for 12 months. Must not have completed any formal education or training resulting in a qualification. For appointment to the position with The College, it is a mandatory requirement for the incumbent of this position to have a current NSW Employee Working with Children Clearance in accordance with the NSW Child Protection (Working with Children) Act 2012. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Community and Connection: Be part of a vibrant Indigenous community with opportunities to connect through staff networks, mentoring, cultural events and Indigenous-led initiatives. Paid Cultural and Ceremonial Leave: Indigenous employees are entitled to 5 days of paid leave and 10 days of unpaid leave each year to participate in cultural and ceremonial activities and fulfil community obligations. Culturally Responsive Wellbeing Support: Access dedicated wellbeing services, including culturally responsive Employee Assistance Program support Indigenous employees and their families. Flexible Work and Exceptional Benefits: Enjoy flexible work arrangements, Fitness Passport, generous leave provisions, staff discounts and access to a wide range of University facilities and services. Application Timeline Advertisement: The job posting will be closing at 11:59pm on Sunday 8th November 2026. Shortlisting: Following the application closing date, all applications will go through a shortlisting process, which can take up to 2 weeks. Interviews: Interviews will be conducted in a face-to-face setting on our Parramatta South Campus. Commencement: The successful applicants will commence in February 2027. Position Enquiries: Please contact Brody O’Brien at B.O’Brien@westernsydney.edu.au for any questions about the position. Please include the job reference code REF1833A in your email. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For reasonable adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Lecturer, Speech Pathology Salary Location Campbelltown, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Campbelltown Business Unit Faculty of Health (U73M) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Fixed-Term position for 2 Years.Based at Campbelltown campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: Academic Level B $125,177 – $147,810 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.NSW Emplo Reference 7c71313c-64b9-4bcc-af6d-74748692279a Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Business Administration Trainee (Indigenous Identified Role) Salary Location Penrith, AU Division Indigenous Leadership Brand Western Sydney University Location Penrith Business Unit Office of the DVC, Indigenous Leadership (U72A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description This is an identified position and applicants must be an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander Person. Being an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person is a genuine occupational qualificati Reference 4ca10447-80d0-4275-943b-b387118539b7 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Business Administration Trainee (Indigenous Identified Role) Salary Location Campbelltown, AU Division Indigenous Leadership Brand Western Sydney University Location Campbelltown Business Unit Office of the DVC, Indigenous Leadership (U72A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description This is an identified position and applicants must be an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander Person. Being an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person is a genuine occupational qualificati Reference 0b38ad18-b844-44c1-bf76-7f6980e37271 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Business Administration Trainee (Indigenous Identified Role) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Indigenous Leadership Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the DVC, Indigenous Leadership (U72A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description This is an identified position and applicants must be an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander Person. Being an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person is a genuine occupational qualificati Reference 439aa37b-e6f1-42b8-976d-39361590d163 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Livestock Coordinator Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Property & Commercial (U76F) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing position Based at Western’s Hawkesbury (Richmond) campus Salary: HEW Level 5 $87,065 – $98,462 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading Manage livestock, pasture and farm operations Reference f423002a-21dd-409f-aedd-cae70054b1df Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Associate Research Fellow - Women's Sexual and Reproductive Health Salary Location Campbelltown, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Campbelltown Business Unit Translational Health Research Institute (U73H) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description 2 Years Fixed-Term position at Academic Level A.Campbelltown campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $98,611 – $119,137 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading Apply inclusive research Reference bd468cb6-9ec3-4ee8-8c35-c01db9177796 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Remuneration & Benefits Specialist Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury and Parramatta South campuses with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead remuner Reference 0ac8e10e-d401-4a3e-9b53-fc5fc92fbefe Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Lecturer (Chemistry) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Engineering, Computing & Science (U73K) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Ongoing position at Academic Level B.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Teach chemistry, d Reference 4ee3304b-a192-44f8-be8d-507908406a1f Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Lecturer in Finance Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Soc.Sciences,Art,Business,Education&Law (U73L) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Fixed-Term position to 30 November 2027 at Academic Level B.Parramatta City Campus.Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape future finance graduates thr Reference 11605e60-54ae-40be-a995-73258a97790b Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Manager, IT Service Management - Digital Services Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead enterprise IT servi Reference 77653bd1-243b-49da-bb96-0a480288384a Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Apply"
